<rml>
<head>
	<title>Mod Library</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="../rcss/menu.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="../rcss/play.rcss"/>
	<style>
		.cols { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 0; bottom: 0; display: flex; padding: 1rem 2.5rem; }
		.main { position: relative; flex: 1; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; margin-right: 2rem; }
		.side { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 26rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 0; }
		.bar { display: flex; align-items: center; }
		.bar .count { margin-left: auto; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #8d847c; }
		/* flex: 1, a zero basis: RmlUi doesn't shrink an auto basis below the rows */
		.list { flex: 1; min-height: 0; overflow-y: auto; margin-top: 0.75rem; border: 1dp #ffffff12; }
		.mrow { position: relative; border-bottom: 1dp #ffffff0d; }
		.mrow .hit { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 0; bottom: 0; transition: background-color 0.1s linear-in-out; }
		.mrow .hit:hover { background-color: #ffffff0a; }
		.mrow .hit:focus { background-color: #db241026; }
		.mrow .cells { position: relative; z-index: 1; display: flex; align-items: center; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; pointer-events: none; }
		.mrow .txt { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
		.mrow .nm { display: flex; align-items: center; }
		.mrow .nm .t { font-family: OzDisplay; font-size: 1.05rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: #fff3e6; }
		.mrow .nm .badge { margin-left: 0.6rem; }
		.mrow .nm .ver { margin-left: 0.6rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: #8d847c; }
		.mrow .sub { margin-top: 0.2rem; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.4; color: #8d847c; }
		.mrow .sub .dir { color: #e6ddd2; }
		.mrow .uses { margin-top: 0.2rem; font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.4; color: #5d554f; }
		.mrow .acts { display: flex; align-items: center; margin-left: 1rem; }
		.mrow .acts button { pointer-events: auto; margin-left: 0.5rem; }
		.badge.ok { border-color: #5ccf4a66; background-color: #5ccf4a1a; color: #5ccf4a; }
		.badge.warn { border-color: #ffd23c66; background-color: #ffd23c1a; color: #ffd23c; }
		.badge.sup { border-color: #4a7dff80; background-color: #4a7dff1a; color: #7d9fff; }
		.emptywrap { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 3rem; bottom: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 1.5rem; }
		.emptywrap .empty { border-color: #ffffff1a; background-color: #00000033; }

		.side .buttons { display: flex; margin-top: 0.75rem; }
		.side .buttons button { margin-right: 0.75rem; }
		.side .drop { margin-top: 0.75rem; padding: 1rem; border: 1dp dashed #ffffff26; border-radius: 2dp; text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.45; color: #8d847c; }
		.side .note { margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.45; color: #5d554f; }
		.side .section { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
		.known { flex: 1; min-height: 0; overflow-y: auto; margin-top: 0.5rem; padding-right: 0.25rem; }
		.krow { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; padding: 0.4rem 0; border-bottom: 1dp #ffffff0a; }
		.krow .kn { width: 9rem; flex: 0 0 auto; font-family: OzDisplay; font-size: 0.8rem; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: #e6ddd2; }
		.krow .kn .d { display: block; margin-top: 0.15rem; font-family: Barlow; font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0; color: #5d554f; }
		.krow .ku { flex: 1; font-size: 0.78rem; line-height: 1.4; color: #8d847c; }
		.krow .kf { flex: 0 0 auto; margin-left: 0.5rem; }

		/* the import card and the remove question, over the list (a modal: the d-pad stays in it) */
		.list.under { visibility: hidden; }
		.card {
			position: absolute;
			left: 4%; right: 4%; top: 12%;
			z-index: 5;
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
			padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
			border: 1dp #db241066;
			background-color: #0a0807f7;
		}
		.card .cname { font-family: OzDisplay; font-size: 1.3rem; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: #fff3e6; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
		.card .mtext { margin-top: 0.6rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.45; color: #e6ddd2; }
		.card .mtext.dim { color: #8d847c; }
		.card .mtext.msg { color: #5ccf4a; }
		.card .mtext.msg.bad { color: #ff4a1c; }
		.card .field { display: flex; align-items: center; margin-top: 0.75rem; }
		.card .field .l { width: 12rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #e6ddd2cc; }
		.card .field input.text { width: 16rem; }
		.card .cfoot { display: flex; margin-top: 1rem; }
		.card .cfoot button { margin-right: 0.75rem; nav-up: none; nav-down: none; }
	</style>
</head>
<!--
The Mod Library (ENGINE_PLAN.md PH step 2; decision 24: players bring their own). Oz never provides
CPMA or Defrag, nor any other mod: no download, no link. The rows are the mod folders found in the
player's user folder (imported) and their Quake III install (oz_mods.c OzMods_List), each with its
version and whether it's ready. Import a zip, a pak or a folder (Windows' open dialog), or drop one
on the game's window: the card guesses the mod's folder name from its paks and imports it into the
user folder. Remove deletes an imported mod's folder. Play opens Skirmish on CPMA or Defrag, or
starts a match under any other mod (its own rules, the Oz HUD, no promise it plays right).
-->
<body data-model="menu">
	<div class="panel">
		<div class="corners"><div class="tl"/><div class="tr"/><div class="bl"/><div class="br"/></div>
		<div class="topline"/>
		<div class="phead">
			<div><banner text="Mod Library"/><p class="subtitle">The mods you bring. Oz finds CPMA, Defrag and the rest in your Quake III folder, and imports what you got yourself: a zip, a pak or a folder, picked or dropped on this window.</p></div>
			<div class="backbtn" onclick="back"><kbd>Esc</kbd><span>Back</span></div>
		</div>
		<div class="divider"/>
		<div class="pbody">
			<div class="cols">
				<div class="main">
					<div class="bar">
						<div class="section first" style="flex: 1; margin-right: 1rem;"><span class="t">Your mods</span><span class="rule"/></div>
						<span class="count">{{ mods.count }}</span>
					</div>
					<div id="ml_list" class="list" data-class-under="mods.ask.open || mods.remove.open">
						<div class="mrow" data-for="m, i : mods.rows">
							<button class="hit" data-attr-id="'ml_row_' + i" data-style-nav-right="'#ml_play_' + i" data-attr-onclick="'modlib_play ' + m.dir"/>
							<div class="cells">
								<div class="txt">
									<div class="nm"><span class="t">{{ m.name }}</span><span class="ver" data-if="m.version != ''">{{ m.version }}</span>
										<span class="badge sup" data-if="m.supported">Supported</span>
										<span class="badge ok" data-if="m.ready">Ready</span>
										<span class="badge warn" data-if="!m.ready">{{ m.state_text }}</span>
										<span class="badge dimb" data-if="m.imported">Imported</span>
									</div>
									<div class="sub"><span class="dir">{{ m.dir }}</span><span>, {{ m.paks }} {{ m.paks == '1' ? 'pak' : 'paks' }}: {{ m.where }}</span></div>
									<div class="uses">{{ m.uses }}</div>
								</div>
								<div class="acts">
									<button class="btn small" data-attr-id="'ml_play_' + i" data-style-nav-left="'#ml_row_' + i" data-style-nav-right="m.imported ? '#ml_remove_' + i : 'none'" data-attr-onclick="'modlib_play ' + m.dir">{{ m.ready ? 'Play' : (m.nested ? 'Import' : 'Play') }}</button>
									<button class="btn small" data-if="m.imported" data-attr-id="'ml_remove_' + i" data-style-nav-left="'#ml_play_' + i" data-attr-onclick="'modlib_remove ' + m.dir">Remove</button>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="emptywrap" data-if="mods.rows.size == 0 &amp;&amp; !mods.ask.open &amp;&amp; !mods.remove.open">
						<div class="empty"><div class="t">No mods found</div><p>No mod folder with paks in your user folder or your Quake III folder. Import one you got yourself, or drop its zip on this window.</p></div>
					</div>

					<!-- the import card (oz_ui_mods.cpp): the file picked or dropped, the folder name guessed for it -->
					<div class="card modal" data-if="mods.ask.open">
						<div class="cname">Import {{ mods.ask.file }}</div>
						<p class="mtext">Its files go into a folder of their own in your user folder, where the game finds them as it finds a mod in your Quake III folder. Programs in it (.exe, .dll) are left out: Oz runs a mod's game code, never its programs.</p>
						<div class="field"><span class="l">The mod's folder name</span><input id="ml_ask_dir" class="text" type="text" maxlength="32" data-value="mods.ask.dir"/></div>
						<p class="mtext msg" data-if="mods.ask.message != ''" data-class-bad="mods.ask.status == 'failed'">{{ mods.ask.message }}</p>
						<div class="cfoot">
							<button id="ml_ask_go" class="btn small primary" data-if="mods.ask.status != 'done'" onclick="modlib_go">Import</button>
							<button id="ml_ask_close" class="btn small" onclick="modlib_close">{{ mods.ask.status == 'done' ? 'Done' : 'Cancel' }}</button>
						</div>
					</div>
					<!-- the remove question -->
					<div class="card modal" data-if="mods.remove.open">
						<div class="cname">Remove {{ mods.remove.name }}?</div>
						<p class="mtext">Its folder in your user folder is deleted, with its settings and demos: {{ mods.remove.where }}</p>
						<p class="mtext dim">A copy in your Quake III folder stays as it is.</p>
						<div class="cfoot">
							<button id="ml_remove_go" class="btn small" onclick="modlib_remove_go">Remove</button>
							<button id="ml_remove_no" class="btn small" onclick="modlib_remove_no">Keep it</button>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="side">
					<div class="section first"><span class="t">Import</span><span class="rule"/></div>
					<div class="buttons">
						<button id="ml_zip" class="btn small primary" autofocus="" onclick="modlib_import zip">Import a zip</button>
						<button id="ml_folder" class="btn small" onclick="modlib_import folder">Import a folder</button>
						<button id="ml_refresh" class="btn small" onclick="modlib_refresh">Look again</button>
					</div>
					<div class="drop">Or drop a mod's zip, pak or folder anywhere on this window.</div>
					<p class="note">Oz never downloads a mod or says where to get one: CPMA and Defrag come from their makers, under their own terms. A server that offers its mod's files hands them over as you join.</p>
					<div class="section"><span class="t">Known mods</span><span class="rule"/></div>
					<div class="known">
						<div class="krow" data-for="k : mods.known">
							<span class="kn">{{ k.name }}<span class="d">{{ k.dir }}</span></span>
							<span class="ku">{{ k.uses }}</span>
							<span class="kf badge ok" data-if="k.found">Found</span>
							<span class="kf badge sup" data-if="!k.found &amp;&amp; k.supported">Supported</span>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
